  "plain": "A radar researcher named Filippo Biondi says that in the 2020s his team changed how they used satellite radar scans so they could see deep below the ground at Giza in Egypt, the site of the great pyramids. With the new setup, he says, they were able to detect and measure structures lying underneath. If true, it would mean there is far more built beneath the pyramids than anyone knows."
